  "notes": "Whole Brussels Town Hall: asymmetrical Gothic front/side wings and steep dormered slate roofs, off-center tall square/octagonal open belfry/spire/corner turrets/pinnacles, physical recessed pointed windows/ground arcade/central passage, original simplified stone tracery/buttresses/balcony/niche mass and gilt finial; intrinsic later rear courtyard wings and covered porticos included with bounded hidden elevations. Native civic front/side outline1228487152 and rear-wing outline23770973 are actual built components; preserve open central courtyard. Named townhall amenity1126164595/Q1255327 establishes identity but includes courtyard/property and must never be extruded as a whole block. Nearby guild houses/GrandPlace/Broodhuis/streets/flags/decor/people/interiors and copied detailed statuary/signs excluded."
